From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 13:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winebus: Prefer HIDRAW for DualShock 4 controllers

Native DualShock 4 devices can currently be published through both HIDRAW and
SDL.  Games using Sony's native pad library may open the SDL copy while output
reports are delivered through the HIDRAW copy, splitting input and rumble
ownership.  Across hotplug this can leave the game with no feedback or replay
a stale high-amplitude motor report.

Use the same policy already used for DualSense: suppress the SDL copy of DS4
v1/v2 and retain the complete physical HIDRAW device.  Steam Input virtual
controllers are unaffected because they use Valve's VID/PID.
---
 dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
@@ -1024,6 +1024,8 @@ static void sdl_add_device(unsigned int index)
-    if (is_dualsense_gamepad(desc.vid, desc.pid))
+    if (is_dualsense_gamepad(desc.vid, desc.pid) ||
+            is_dualshock4_gamepad(desc.vid, desc.pid))
     {
-        TRACE("ignoring SDL DualSense device %s; hidraw handles native reports.\n", debugstr_device_desc(&desc));
+        TRACE("ignoring SDL Sony controller %s; hidraw handles native reports.\n",
+                debugstr_device_desc(&desc));
         if (controller) pSDL_GameControllerClose(controller);
         pSDL_JoystickClose(joystick);
         return;
